#pragma once
#include <cstdint>

// Soft-edged white circle, 6x6 RGBA -- matches DOT_RADIUS*2 exactly, so
// it's drawn 1:1 at its native size, no runtime scaling at all. Used as
// the dot sprite for zone overlay dots (see PrimAddFilledDotSprite in
// worldrender.cpp). White RGB so it tints to each zone's configured
// color via vertex color.
//
// Generated by supersampling a hard-edged circle at 48x resolution and
// area-average downsampling to 6x6 (Pillow's BOX filter) -- the
// antialiasing comes from that downsample step (a real per-texel
// coverage average), not from anything inherent to the PNG format
// itself, and not from a hand-derived radial alpha formula either.
//
// If DOT_RADIUS in worldrender.cpp ever changes, this sprite must be
// regenerated at 2*DOT_RADIUS and kDotQuadHalfSize updated to match.
// 113 bytes
